<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="How Surya Tech Codex handles analytics, comments, cookies, and information shared by visitors.">
  <article class="legal-page shell">
    <header><span class="kicker">Trust and transparency</span><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p>Effective 21 August 2026 · Last updated 21 August 2026</p></header>
    <div class="legal-content">
      <section><h2>Overview</h2><p>Surya Tech Codex is a personal technology publication operated by Suryakant. This policy explains what information may be processed when you visit the website and the choices available to you.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Information collected automatically</h2><p>If you accept analytics, Google Analytics may process information such as pages viewed, approximate location, device and browser type, traffic source, interactions, and a pseudonymous identifier. We use this information in aggregate to understand readership and improve articles. We do not intentionally send names, email addresses, phone numbers, or other directly identifying information to Google Analytics.</p><p>Google Analytics uses first-party cookies, including <code>_ga</code>. The Analytics tag is blocked until you select “Accept analytics.” If you decline, no Google Analytics tag is loaded by this website.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Consent and cookie preferences</h2><p>Your analytics choice is stored in your browser’s local storage so the website can remember it. You can change that choice at any time by selecting <button type="button" class="inline-preference" data-open-consent>Cookie preferences</button> in the footer or on this page. Clearing this website’s browser storage will also reset the choice.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Comments and reactions</h2><p>Article discussions are provided by Giscus and GitHub Discussions. If you choose to comment or react, GitHub processes that activity under its own account terms and privacy policy. Surya Tech Codex does not receive your GitHub password.</p></section>
      <section><h2>External services and links</h2><p>The website may link to GitHub, LinkedIn, Feedly, Inoreader, WordPress, YouTube, and other third-party services. Their privacy practices apply when you visit or interact with them.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Data retention and security</h2><p>Analytics retention is managed in the Google Analytics property. Reasonable technical measures are used to protect the website, but no internet service can guarantee absolute security. We do not sell personal information.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Your choices</h2><p>You may decline analytics, withdraw consent, use browser privacy controls, or contact us with a privacy question. Depending on where you live, additional access, correction, deletion, or objection rights may apply.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Contact</h2><p>For privacy questions, email <a href="mailto:suryatechcodex@gmail.com">suryatechcodex@gmail.com</a>.</p></section>
      <aside class="legal-note">This policy may be updated when the website or its services change. The effective date above will be revised when material updates are made.</aside>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
